## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the project.

### What Was Implemented

1. **Package Installation**
   - Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
   - Updated package.json and package-lock.json accordingly

2. **Analytics Integration**
   - Added Analytics component to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`)
   - Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next`
   - Placed the `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag, following Vercel's official documentation

### Files Modified

- **frontend/package.json** - Added `@vercel/analytics` dependency
- **frontend/package-lock.json** - Updated with new dependency tree
- **frontend/src/app/layout.tsx** - Added Analytics import and component

### Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Fetched latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Used framework-specific setup for Next.js App Router
- Analytics component is placed after all providers but before closing body tag for optimal loading
- The Analytics component automatically handles route tracking and visitor data collection

### Technical Notes

- This is a Next.js 16.2.11 App Router project using TypeScript
- The Analytics component is a client-side component that won't impact SSR or initial page load
- Analytics will start collecting data once the app is deployed to Vercel and Analytics is enabled in the Vercel dashboard
- No additional configuration is needed; the component works out of the box

### Build Status

- The linter ran successfully with no errors introduced by our changes
- Pre-existing linting warnings remain unchanged
- The project has a pre-existing Firebase configuration issue (invalid API key) that prevents a full production build, but this is unrelated to the Analytics integration
- TypeScript compilation of the modified layout.tsx file is valid

### Next Steps for Deployment

To enable analytics data collection:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the project's Analytics section
3. Once deployed, verify the Analytics component is working by checking for Fetch/XHR requests in the browser's Network tab

The integration is complete and ready for deployment.
